Griabuntu Mail is an independent private downstream of Convey 51.0, itself
derived from Geary. Original authorship, copyright and notices are retained
in individual files, AUTHORS, THANKS and the original Git history.

This elected application source copy and the new debian/ packaging are licensed
under GNU GPL version 3 only. See COPYING and docs/release/GPLV3-COPY.md.
On Debian/Ubuntu, the complete GPLv3 text is also available at
/usr/share/common-licenses/GPL-3.

This is not a blanket licence for every file. The repository's
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md, COPYING.icons, COPYING.sounds and docs/licenses/ retain
component-specific copyright notices and licence texts. These are installed
under /usr/share/licenses/io.github.d3rpapah0d3n.GriabuntuMail/ by the application build.
The original LGPL reference is preserved as COPYING.LGPL-2.1-original.
In particular, bundled Dark Reader is MIT, ValaUnit remains LGPL, the Snowball
binding retains its BSD notice, and icon/sound/brand assets retain their
individual CC or LGPL terms. System libraries are separate Ubuntu packages;
their notices are available in their respective /usr/share/doc directories.

This local preview does not close the inherited asset/source/provenance and
public-name work listed in RELEASE-CHECKLIST.md. It is not a public release.

The 2026-10-27 original Griabuntu Mail envelope icon family is CC0-1.0,
with exact files/provenance listed in the installed Griabuntu-Mail-Artwork.md
and full text in Griabuntu-Mail-Artwork-CC0-1.0.txt. Older inherited icon
artwork remains in source history/archives under its original terms.
